# BUG-261 regression: a `use` that resolves to a sibling .c must link and call.
# Also pins BUG-258 (`extern` was in the grammar but rejected by the parser): this
# file cannot even parse if `extern def` stops being accepted at top level.
#
# THIS FIXTURE MUST RUN, NOT MERELY COMPILE. The whole failure mode of FFI is a
# declaration that resolves to nothing or to the wrong ABI, and both of those
# produce Zig that passes semantic analysis. compile_check and full_sweep build
# with `-fno-emit-bin`, so they never link this and cannot see either. Only the
# smoke_run registration (asserting the printed 42) actually exercises it.
#
# It also pins the emit shape that BUG-261 got wrong: `use cprobe_add3` must
# NOT become `@import("cprobe_add3.zig")`, because no such file exists.
#
# ABI note: the C side takes three `int`, so the Zebra declaration says `int32`.
# Writing `int` would be an i64/c_int mismatch that links cleanly and corrupts
# the call -- green build, wrong program.

use cprobe_add3

extern def zebra_probe_add3(a: int32, b: int32, c: int32): int32

def main()
    print(zebra_probe_add3(20, 20, 2))
